# Round q38ref: ik's CPU node dumps of the Qwen3.8-Flash-Next UD-Q4_K_XL split set (four shards,
# 111,334,654,784 B), each one `just dump-ref-qwen4exp [VARIANT]` under this card: the batch set, then
# step4, step4-every-node, d1k and d3k, one lease each, back to back. dump_ref loads without
# --defer-experts, so ik's loader populates every shard in turn (one stream), then computes on 32
# threads, then writes the nodes to /root/bloomery-data. The three phases run one after the other: the
# wall is their sum. The one term the batch dump fixes: this file's cold-read rate through the loader's
# populate, read from the witness block's read-sectors and wall; the step dumps then read nothing
# from the device unless a run between two dumps evicted the file.
# Seconds per dump [derived], scaled from glmref's measured GLM dumps (199.7 GB: batch cold 133 s,
# step4-every-node warm 17 s, d1k warm 29 s; commit 0b5d1c9):
#   populate  cold: 111.3 GB at 1.5-1.72 GB/s (GLM's whole-window and populate-only rates) 65-74 s; at
#             the single-stream priors 1.07-1.33 GB/s 84-104 s. Warm: GLM's 17 s scaled by size <= 10 s
#   fixed     lease, witnesses, metadata over four shards, context: 3-15 s
#   compute   ~13 GFLOP a token (6.6 B active: 36 GDN layers 57.7 M, 12 GQA layers 49.8 M, 48 MoE
#             layers of 11 experts at ff 640 plus the router 55 M, HC ~13 M a layer, output 636 M) at
#             1.25 TFLOP/s (qwen35moe's measured 1,024-token prefill, the same GDN + MoE shape) to
#             3 TFLOP/s (GLM's d1k): batch and step4 < 1 s; d1k 13.5 TFLOP 4.5-10.8 s; d3k 3,000
#             tokens ~41 TFLOP (attention over up to 3,000 cells adds ~1.3) 14-33 s
#   dump      2-4 GB a set (qwen35moe's sets 1.5-1.6 GB at 40 layers, hidden 2048; this model 48 layers,
#             hidden 2560, a 4-stream residual) at 0.5 GB/s: 4-8 s
#   batch cold 72-128 s (1.2-2.1 min); step4, step4-every-node warm 10-20 s; d1k 15-31 s; d3k 24-53 s;
#   the sitting 2.2-4.2 min. A step dump that reads the file from the device again costs the populate
#   term again (65-104 s); all five cold is at most 11 min.
kind: exclusive
reason: dump_ref runs ik on 32 CPU threads and populates the whole 111.3 GB split set into the page
  cache, evicting that much of what else is cached (the V4.1 host set or the GLM set among it); beside
  a timed run or a gate batch it would take their cores, their memory bandwidth and their cache, so it
  holds the lease; why now: the qwen4exp oracle the Qwen3.8 program's e2e gate is judged against
  (round q38ref)
minutes: 0.2..2.2
